            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0501" n="489" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg489"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">585.61B1/592: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-26T15:00:00+02:00">July 26, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 26—10:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3218. The Department’s telegram 2699, July 21, regarding load lines was explained
                    urgently to the Foreign Office on July 22. On July 24 the Foreign Office stated
                    orally that after a meeting of the highest British authorities concerned it was
                    not found possible to agree to the Department’s plan. A long explanatory note
                    has just been received from the Foreign Office embodying draft of a note British
                    Government proposes to send to signatories with whom it has diplomatic relations
                    inviting assent to a declaration modifying the convention to permit loading (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) to tropical marks instead of summer marks and
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) to fresh water tropical marks instead of
                    existing tropical marks.</p>
                <p>Copies will be sent by air pouch 28th.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d495-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
